# The MCUboot image-signing PRIVATE KEY lives in this directory and is never
# committed. It is the only thing deciding what this lock will boot: MCUboot
# embeds the public half and refuses any image the private half did not sign.
# Commit it and anyone can sign firmware your lock accepts.
#
# `make dfu-key` generates one. README.md says what losing it costs.
# Deny by default, then allow back the two files that only describe the
# directory. Listing extensions instead was the old shape and it cannot be made
# complete -- .p12, .pfx, .jks, a DER blob named "signing-key" with no extension
# at all -- and one miss here commits the key that decides what this lock boots.
# Anything genuinely publishable (a public half, a generated header) has to be
# un-ignored on purpose, by name, which is the right amount of friction.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
*.pem
